 "blurb": "Shows the shot as a reel of rotting nitrate film. Pools of decomposed emulsion eat into the picture with bubbled, crystalline edges and a brown crust, leaving a pale amber hollow where the image has gone or a dark sludge where it has rotted, and the picture around them is smeared where the emulsion slid. Every film frame rotted a little differently, so as the clip plays the pools boil and jump the way they do in old archive reels.",
